<!--
    Carcass yield for deliveries to production butchers and contract slaughterhouses
    (Hof Bergmann's farm butcher and public slaughterhouse), in "typical animals": the units a
    facility is configured for per head.

        reference = the animal's own target weight x maleMaturity (or femaleMaturity)
        size      = clamp((reference / anchorWeight) ^ sizeExponent, minSizeFactor, maxSizeFactor)
        finish    = clamp((live weight / reference) ^ finishExponent, minFinishFactor, maxFinishFactor)
        yield     = size x finish x carcassFactor x (1 + qualitySwing x (meat gene - 1))

    The animal's own target weight is its breed's, moved by its metabolism gene. Maturity is the
    share of it a typical slaughter animal of that sex has reached: a finished steer or young
    bull, a cull cow. So a large-framed breed finished to its reference yields more than a small
    one, but less than in proportion to weight, and an animal short of its reference yields less.

    anchorWeight   The reference weight that counts as size 1.
    referenceWeight  Optional: a fixed reference in kg, used instead of target weight x maturity.
    carcassFactor  Breed carcass merit (dressing, muscling, meat value).
    qualitySwing   Yield change per unit of the meat gene (0.25 - 1.75, 1 = average).
    dressingRate   Animal type only: share of the live weight that is carcass (cattle 0.60).
    saleableRate   Animal type only: share of the carcass that is sold on as the map's meat products
                   (cattle 0.75). anchorWeight x dressingRate x saleableRate is the meat one typical
                   animal gives: a 600 kg standard cow -> 360 kg carcass -> 270 kg of meat, a 125 kg
                   pig -> 75 kg, a 42.67 kg lamb -> 19.2 kg (x 0.50 x 0.90), a 3 kg bird -> 1.89 kg.
    meatPerHead    Animal type only: kg of meat one typical animal gives, instead of the two rates.
                   The meat of a typical animal is what every facility is set to: a contract
                   slaughterhouse's recipe (Hof Bergmann's public one) is rescaled to it at load, and
                   a unit-based farm butcher is credited units x its recipe ratio = meatPerHead per
                   typical animal, whatever unitsPerAnimal and recipe the map ships. A type without it
                   keeps the facility's own recipe.

    processingFeePerKg  Animal type only: fine cutting and packing to the map's sellable meat, charged per kg
                   on top of the slaughterhouse's own fee (cattle 0.37, pigs 0.60, sheep 1.20; poultry and
                   rabbits 0, sold whole). It is added to the contract
                   slaughterhouse's fee per batch at load, so it is paid through the same order and fee
                   budget; the map is not edited. A type without it is not charged.
    slaughterFee   Animal type only: the map's fee per typical animal (cattle 100, pig 50, sheep 40,
                   poultry and rabbit 5), used to price the floor.
    A meat animal's live price is its curve price x a market factor (RLMeatValue.getMarketFactor):
        net(price) = meat of a typical animal x price - slaughterFee - processingFeePerKg x that meat
        factor     = 1 + marketPassThrough x (net(current best meat price) / net(annual mean price) - 1)
    kept between marketFactorMin and marketFactorMax. The annual mean price is read from the map: the
    best selling point's price x the mean of the meat's 12 seasonal factors x the difficulty
    multiplier. So the factor is 1 in an average month, and at a pass-through under 1 the live price
    moves less than the meat: slaughtering by contract pays about 0% in the cheapest month, about +12%
    over the year and about +22% at the peak (cattle 0.6). Male animals only unless marketFemales is 1
    (pigs, rabbits: both sexes are fattened); cows, ewes, does and laying birds follow their own curve.
    marketPassThrough  Share of the meat market's move passed to the live price (0.6).
    marketFemales      1: the market factor applies to females too.
    referencePrice     Optional: a fixed annual mean meat price per kg instead of the map's.

    The live sale price has a floor at what slaughtering the animal pays (RLMeatValue). For a type with
    processingFeePerKg:
        value = (meat kg x best current meat price - slaughterFee x yield - processingFeePerKg x meat kg)
                / (1 + maxSlaughterMargin)
    so slaughtering by contract never earns more than maxSlaughterMargin over selling live, even under
    great demand or for a heavy, high-quality animal: the arbitrage cap. Other types use
    meat x price x slaughterShare.

    meatFillType   Animal type only: the fill type its meat sells as. None, or one the map lacks,
                   means no floor.
    maxSlaughterMargin  The most slaughtering by contract earns over selling live (cattle 0.25).
    cullFloorFactor  From cullAgeMonth on the floor is multiplied by this (an old cow or bull).
    slaughterShare Share of its meat's value an animal fetches live (types without processingFeePerKg). The rest is the processing
                   margin you keep by slaughtering yourself.
    cullShare      The same from cullAgeMonth on: an old cow or bull, sow or boar, or mutton sells
                   as low-grade processing meat.
    cullAgeMonth   Age in months from which cullShare applies. None means never.
    slaughterMinAgeMonth  No floor below this age (the butcher takes none younger).
    facilityMinAgeMonth  Animal type only: the youngest age every butcher and contract slaughterhouse takes the
                   type at, written over the map's own minimum when the placeable is added (RLFacilityAge).
                   None keeps the map's.

    Each of these is looked up by subType name first, then by breed within the animal type, then
    by animal type, then on the carcassYield element. A type with no anchorWeight uses the mean
    target weight of the subtypes the facility takes as the same fill type.

    To change these without editing the mod, copy this file to
    modSettings/FS25_RealisticLivestockF2M/carcassYield.xml; that copy then replaces this file
    entirely. In multiplayer the server's file applies.
-->
<carcassYield qualitySwing="0.20" slaughterShare="0.85" cullShare="0.70" maxSlaughterMargin="0.25" cullFloorFactor="0.82"
              sizeExponent="0.25" minSizeFactor="0.88" maxSizeFactor="1.15"
              finishExponent="0.85" minFinishFactor="0" maxFinishFactor="1.3">
    <animalType name="COW" anchorWeight="600" dressingRate="0.60" saleableRate="0.75" slaughterFee="100" processingFeePerKg="0.37" marketPassThrough="0.6" marketFactorMin="0.5" marketFactorMax="1.5" meatFillType="BEEFMEAT" cullAgeMonth="30" slaughterMinAgeMonth="6" maleMaturity="0.75" femaleMaturity="0.90">
        <breed name="HOLSTEIN"      maleMaturity="0.59" femaleMaturity="0.85" carcassFactor="0.94"/>
        <breed name="SWISS_BROWN"   maleMaturity="0.62" femaleMaturity="0.85" carcassFactor="0.98"/>
        <breed name="HEREFORD"      maleMaturity="0.60" carcassFactor="1.00"/>
        <breed name="ANGUS"         maleMaturity="0.60" carcassFactor="1.06"/>
        <breed name="LIMOUSIN"      maleMaturity="0.585" carcassFactor="1.06"/>
        <breed name="HIGHLAND"      maleMaturity="0.615" carcassFactor="1.01"/>
        <breed name="WATER_BUFFALO" maleMaturity="0.625" carcassFactor="0.94"/>
    </animalType>

    <!-- Finishing pigs: a 125 kg pig x 0.80 to the carcass x 0.75 to sellable pork = 75 kg. Gilts are finished
         like barrows, so the pork market moves their live price too (marketFemales). Finished at 6 months
         (6.5 Berkshire), the map's youngest age for the butcher. Maturity = finishing weight / mature weight. -->
    <animalType name="PIG" anchorWeight="125" dressingRate="0.80" saleableRate="0.75" slaughterFee="50" processingFeePerKg="0.60" marketPassThrough="0.6" marketFactorMin="0.5" marketFactorMax="1.5" marketFemales="1" meatFillType="PORKMEAT" cullAgeMonth="12" slaughterMinAgeMonth="6">
        <breed name="LANDRACE"   maleMaturity="0.39"  femaleMaturity="0.446" carcassFactor="1.00"/>  <!-- 125 kg -->
        <breed name="BERKSHIRE"  maleMaturity="0.40"  femaleMaturity="0.50"  carcassFactor="1.08"/>  <!-- 120 kg -->
        <breed name="BLACK_PIED" maleMaturity="0.444" femaleMaturity="0.60"  carcassFactor="0.96"/>  <!-- 120 kg -->
    </animalType>

    <!-- Lambs (sheep S3, 2026-10-11): the cattle chain's sellable share, 270 kg of a 600 kg cow = 0.45, as dressing 0.50
         (LfL: 48-52% at 42 kg) x sellable 0.90. A typical lamb is 42.67 kg (the real market lamb, "about 42 kg"), so it
         still gives 19.2 kg. Each breed's ram lamb is finished at its real market weight (maleMaturity = market weight /
         the ram's target weight): 42.7 kg lowland and terminal breeds, 38 kg hill breeds, Black Welsh 35.4 kg (14-19 kg
         carcass). Butchers and the slaughterhouse take sheep from 3 months (facilityMinAgeMonth; AHDB: early lambs on
         concentrate are finished at 12-14 weeks), over the map's 8. Ewes and does are culled grown. Goats share the SHEEP
         type and so its 3-month minimum (meat kids are finished at 3-6 months; decided 2026-10-13), but keep their own
         anchor of 50 kg and their buck kid line (35 kg at 8 months), so a 35 kg kid still gives
         19.2 x (35/50)^0.25 x 0.94 = 16.5 kg. -->
    <animalType name="SHEEP" anchorWeight="42.6667" dressingRate="0.50" saleableRate="0.90" slaughterFee="40" processingFeePerKg="1.20" marketPassThrough="0.6" marketFactorMin="0.5" marketFactorMax="1.5" meatFillType="SHEEPGOATMEAT" cullAgeMonth="12" slaughterMinAgeMonth="3" facilityMinAgeMonth="3" femaleMaturity="0.85">
        <breed name="LANDRACE"             maleMaturity="0.296" carcassFactor="1.00"/>  <!-- 42.7 kg -->
        <breed name="STEINSCHAF"           maleMaturity="0.507" carcassFactor="1.02"/>  <!-- 38 kg -->
        <breed name="SWISS_MOUNTAIN"       maleMaturity="0.395" carcassFactor="1.04"/>  <!-- 42.7 kg -->
        <breed name="BLACK_WELSH"          maleMaturity="0.521" carcassFactor="1.00"/>  <!-- 35.4 kg -->
        <breed name="TEXEL"                maleMaturity="0.427"/>  <!-- 42.7 kg -->
        <breed name="SUFFOLK"              maleMaturity="0.427"/>  <!-- 42.7 kg -->
        <breed name="BLUE_FACED_LEICESTER" maleMaturity="0.464"/>  <!-- 42.7 kg -->
        <breed name="BORDER_LEICESTER"     maleMaturity="0.427"/>  <!-- 42.7 kg -->
        <breed name="BELCLARE"             maleMaturity="0.496"/>  <!-- 42.7 kg -->
        <breed name="DORSET"               maleMaturity="0.508"/>  <!-- 42.7 kg -->
        <breed name="CHEVIOT"              maleMaturity="0.521"/>  <!-- 38 kg -->
        <breed name="KERRY_HILL"           maleMaturity="0.521"/>  <!-- 38 kg -->
        <breed name="NORFOLK"              maleMaturity="0.521"/>  <!-- 38 kg -->
        <breed name="BLACKFACE"            maleMaturity="0.487"/>  <!-- 38 kg -->
        <breed name="EASYCARE"             maleMaturity="0.533"/>  <!-- 42.7 kg -->
        <breed name="JACOB"                maleMaturity="0.594"/>  <!-- 38 kg -->
        <breed name="GOAT"                 anchorWeight="50" maleMaturity="0.389" carcassFactor="0.94" qualitySwing="0.12"/>  <!-- 35 kg -->
    </animalType>

    <!-- Poultry and rabbits are sold whole: dressed bird or rabbit x 0.90 sellable. The map's fee of 5 per head
         covers the slaughter; no cutting fee. Cockerels, drakes and ganders are the meat animals (hens, ducks and
         geese lay); both sexes of rabbit are fattened. The butcher's youngest ages are the map's.
         The butcher takes no horses, so the slaughterhouse keeps its own horse recipe. -->
    <animalType name="HORSE" anchorWeight="550"/>
    <animalType name="CHICKEN" anchorWeight="3.0" dressingRate="0.70" saleableRate="0.90" slaughterFee="5" processingFeePerKg="0" marketPassThrough="0.6" marketFactorMin="0.5" marketFactorMax="1.5" meatFillType="POULTRYMEAT" cullAgeMonth="18" slaughterMinAgeMonth="6" maleMaturity="0.753" femaleMaturity="0.90">  <!-- ducks share the type on Hof Bergmann -->
        <!-- a cockerel 3.2 kg at 6 months, a spent hen at 90% of grown -->
        <breed name="DUCK" maleMaturity="0.905"/>  <!-- 3.8 kg drake at 6 months -->
    </animalType>
    <animalType name="GOOSE" anchorWeight="7.0" dressingRate="0.70" saleableRate="0.90" slaughterFee="5" processingFeePerKg="0" marketPassThrough="0.6" marketFactorMin="0.5" marketFactorMax="1.5" meatFillType="GOOSEMEAT" cullAgeMonth="24" slaughterMinAgeMonth="10" maleMaturity="0.90" femaleMaturity="0.90"/>  <!-- 7.2 kg gander at 10 months -->
    <animalType name="RABBIT" anchorWeight="3.0" dressingRate="0.58" saleableRate="0.90" slaughterFee="5" processingFeePerKg="0" marketPassThrough="0.6" marketFactorMin="0.5" marketFactorMax="1.5" marketFemales="1" meatFillType="RABBITMEAT" cullAgeMonth="12" slaughterMinAgeMonth="4" maleMaturity="0.652" femaleMaturity="0.60"/>  <!-- 3 kg at 4 months -->

    <!-- Example of a single subtype:
    <subType name="BULL_HIGHLAND_CATTLE" maleMaturity="0.80"/>
    -->
</carcassYield>
